<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  CycloneDDS profile for the SJTU simulator container, written for exactly one
  job: being visible to the ROS 1 <-> ROS 2 bridge, which runs Foxy.

  Why CycloneDDS at all. Humble ships Fast DDS 2.6 and Foxy ships Fast DDS 2.1.
  The two are not wire-compatible, so a Humble publisher and a Foxy subscriber
  on the same domain discover nothing and report nothing -- it looks exactly
  like a dead node. CycloneDDS on both sides is the combination that works.

  Why SharedMemory is off. Humble's CycloneDDS enables the iceoryx shared-memory
  transport by default; Foxy's CycloneDDS predates it entirely. A sample handed
  to iceoryx never reaches the network, so the bridge sees a discovered,
  connected, permanently silent topic. This is the failure that presents as
  "the bridge lists /simple_drone/odom but rostopic hz says no new messages".

  Why AllowMulticast is spdp and not false. SPDP participant discovery needs
  multicast; user data then goes unicast. Do NOT pin NetworkInterfaceAddress to
  "lo" to keep traffic local -- loopback is not multicast-capable, so discovery
  between containers stops dead. Every participant here runs with --net=host and
  shares the host stack, so the default interface is already the right one.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <General>
      <AllowMulticast>spdp</AllowMulticast>
    </General>
    <SharedMemory>
      <Enable>false</Enable>
    </SharedMemory>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
